Netflix public-content integration (2026-11-05):
  Flow research reference: Kiko023/Netflix-DL (NFripper)
  Commit 7f498722d5c915ddac39b25276d266c0ea1ead5c
  https://github.com/Kiko023/Netflix-DL/tree/7f498722d5c915ddac39b25276d266c0ea1ead5c
  Reviewed its cookie/metadata, manifest, download and remux flow. No source code,
  CDMs, device identities, account credentials or keys are copied or distributed.
  Its member MSL/DRM flow is not implemented by this integration.

  netflix_public.go independently downloads original MP4 objects from Netflix's
  public Open Content bucket, with HTTPS bucket restrictions, complete-object
  length checks, local FFprobe inspection and atomic publication.
  Official content source and asset licensing information:
  https://opencontent.netflix.com/
  Netflix states that its Open Content assets are available under CC BY 4.0.
  Cosmos Laundromat is an open movie by the Blender Foundation; this integration
  tests the publicly supplied Netflix SDR encode. Downloaded media is not included
  in the software distribution and retains its original content rights.

Bilibili bangumi integration (2026-11-05):
  Local protocol reference: findrss-scripts/rss/bilibili.js, version 1.1.0.
  Its official metadata/playurl request patterns and scoped cookie handling were
  reviewed. bilibili.go independently implements official PGC season/playurl
  metadata, EP/CID and duration checks, trailer exclusion and DASH track selection.
  media_tracks.go reuses the existing bounded CDN transport/retries, verifies
  complete track sizes and optional publisher MD5 values, and copies local
  audio/video streams into a validated MP4 before atomic publication.
  No JavaScript source, browser fingerprint, account cookie or media key is copied.
